content:
The requested certificate cannot be supplied from the stated construction. A valid example would disprove the open complex Jacobian conjecture in dimension three.

Moreover, the reference map does not satisfy its own Jacobian requirement. On the line \((x,y,z)=(1,0,t)\), its Jacobian matrix is
\[
\begin{pmatrix}
0&3t&1\\
3t&1&3\\
2-3t&-3&-1
\end{pmatrix},
\]
whose determinant is
\[
-18t^2+12t-2=-2(3t-1)^2.
\]
Thus the determinant is \(-2\) at \(t=0\), \(-8\) at \(t=1\), and \(0\) at \(t=\frac13\). The given points do have a common image, but the map is not an admissible constant-Jacobian counterexample.

